# Keep the Dagger context mount small — these never need to enter a gate.
.git
# Local env files (gitignored runtime artifacts holding dev secrets) must never
# enter a gate. Dagger does NOT honor .gitignore, so exclude them explicitly —
# otherwise a locally-created backend/.env trips the gitleaks gate (and makes the
# security result depend on local state). .env.example IS committed + scanned.
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
node_modules
**/node_modules
# Stale nested workspace lockfiles. npm workspaces uses the ROOT lock — the
# Dockerfile, Makefile, and CI all run root `npm ci`, so these are never
# consulted by the build/deploy. They're frozen at old versions and only
# produce trivy false-positives; the security gate must reflect the deployed
# artifact (the root lock). (Cruft worth deleting from the repo too — see CI.md.)
backend/package-lock.json
frontend/package-lock.json
dist
**/dist
build
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.playwright-mcp
ci/sdk
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.mp4
**/*.webm
